  "thesis": "The public rental tape is split: marketplace 1x H100s still print cheap; committed H100/H200/B200 clusters and NVL72 offtake are scarce (SemiAnalysis Apr 2026; CoreWeave Aug 2026 sold-out after a ~25% July raise).",
  "rank_formula": "score = 0.40*liquidity + 0.35*demand + 0.25*frontier; each component 0–3. Scores are ordinal hygiene, not a valuation.",
  "methodology": "Display price prefers a labeled SemiAnalysis 1y contract when one exists (H100). Otherwise a labeled on-demand print from the most liquid public neocloud (Lambda, else CoreWeave). When OD is contact-sales, a labeled spot print may be the display (B300). CNY prints stay CNY-primary (Ascend 910C) with a dated PBOC USD label — no guessed FX. Token/enterprise SKUs (Cerebras, Groq) carry no invented $/hour. A second venue is shown in the row and never blended into the headline number. Capacity Blocks, marketplace floors, and on-demand are incompatible terms. SemiAnalysis public prints stop at April 2026 and are labeled as such. August 2026 figures are neocloud and hyperscaler list pages fetched 2026-08-18. No market-cap, no 7d/30d change, no invented chips.",
  "display_convention": "Prefer labeled 1y if SemiAnalysis has one. Else labeled on-demand from Lambda or CoreWeave. Always show at least one other venue when a second sourced print exists. Never average incompatible terms.",
